A||||9||gixxer||Sent a Mustang to the Glue Factory||||1||
Z||000000||gixxer||04-19-2001||10:21 PM||||Coming home from work today, I lined up next to a late model Mustang with "4.6" on the fender and nice looking wide (stock) rims and tires.<BR>He gave no indication that he wanted to race until the light turned green and he left with a small amount of wheelspin.<BR>I had the clutch out at about 1500 RPMs and was basically caught flat-footed, and the Mustang had about a 1 1/2 lengths on me.<BR>So I floored it and dipped the clutch and popped it back out.<BR>This pretty much lit both the tires up and it hit the rev limiter within a second or so in first. Shifted to 2nd, passed him, shifted to third and ran it to 70 MPH or so.<BR>When I backed off, I was about 2 car lengths ahead and going about 5 MPH faster.<BR>He stayed behind me till he turned off. Don't think he knew what hit him. =)<BR>I was so pleased with my Fiero I gave it a wash.<BR>Luv that turbo!||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||04-20-2001||12:04 AM||||Hehe love those bedtime stories.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Cameron||04-20-2001||03:39 AM||||hehe that is a good story.  unfortunately, for those of us that have horses the term glue factory is a bit upsetting...but when used in the same sentence as mustang and not refuring to the horses I can let it slip by.  Hehe...j/k.  Glad you smoked the stang.<P><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spektyr||04-20-2001||04:19 AM||||Um... I beat an 82 V6 Mustang... hehe.<P>But then my car is stock, so it's a pretty straight fight.  Pulled up next to an 88 Mustang GT about 40 minutes later... sigh.<P>Don't suppose anyone has a turbo V6 laying around they'd let me have so I don't have to keep a low profile around those guys.  (smirk)<P>Didn't think so.  Gotta keep on saving.<P>"One day it will be mine - Oh yes!  It will be mine."  - Wayne in 'Waynes World'<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||14
Z||000004||onfire||04-20-2001||04:22 AM||||You wouldn't happen to drive a silver GT with tinted windows and quarter windows, would you? The Fiero also had a bra and a luggage rack, instead of a spoiler. If so I seen you on I-5 going south around the Sea-Tac area. All the way to Seattle, I took the Spokane street exit.<P>I also seen a maroon GT with T-tops a week ago. Must be spring time.||||reg||1
